  <Index>k__BackingField: 3
  <Name>k__BackingField: Bounded Offsets
  _description: "By default the pivot is placed relative to the bounds of the object. A value of -1 puts it at one end, 0 places it at center, 1 at the opposite end. \n\nTry switching between the cactus and the screw and watch the pivot re-adjust itself to each one.\n\n<color=orange>New</color>\nThe four buttons beside each slider are quick-align shortcuts. The yellow one snaps the handle back to the object's real pivot; the other three jump straight to -1, 0 and 1 on that axis."
  _isNewInV11: 1
